 "limitations": "(1) Every D=8 quantity in this card is OBSERVED-DERIVABLE from l216/static.json and l217/static.json and is scored as DESCRIPTION (PREREG 0b); only the D>8 rates, D*, and the p-values read at D* have a null that was unknown at registration. (2) The existence rate is monotone non-decreasing in D BY CONSTRUCTION (cumulative ANY), so the plateau is a LEVEL statement and the monotonicity is an assert, not a finding. (3) A plateau reached only AFTER the per-cell saturation depth is numerically forced rather than structural: the stored saturation_depth field is what distinguishes the two, and the Q1 record carries plateau_numerically_forced. (4) The null is L205's within-pool side-label permutation; it holds per-side counts exact and relocates nothing else, so it cannot speak to reconstruction completeness (L231's caveat). (5) The 12-test family is the registered one; tests whose REAL event does not exist within D* are scored FALSE BY UNMEASURABILITY and excluded from BH, which SHRINKS m and therefore LOOSENS every bar \u2014 m_measurable is stored beside m_registered. (6) p_omni and every rate share one resolution floor 1/(NDRAW+1) = 4.9975e-04; a p AT the floor is reported as '<= floor', never as a point value.",
